      "claim": "Other human or predicted-human oral bioavailability reports are above threshold: irbesartan 60–82%, anlotinib estimated 41–77%, urapidil slow-release 72%, ranolazine slow-release 35–50%, and ONO-4641 predicted F = 0.710.",
      "card_ids": ["C01","C02","C07","C12","C10","C18","C09","C04","C03","C11","C17"]
    },
    {
      "claim": "L3 oral exposure records for nobiletin and ACT-280778 show low pg/mL Cmax/AUC values but lack matched IV comparators and are for structurally unrelated reference molecules; they do not provide affirmative F < 20% evidence for the query.",
      "card_ids": ["C25","C26","C27","C28","C29","C30","C31","C32","C33","C34","C35","C36"]
    }
  ],
  "new_evidence_assessment": [
    {
      "family": "oral_auc_cmax_exposure",
      "applicability": "low",
      "direction": "neutral_or_unclear",
      "decision_effect": "no_change",
      "card_ids": ["C25","C26","C27","C28","C29","C30","C31","C32","C33","C34","C35","C36"]
    }
  ],
  "evidence_gaps": [
    "No query-specific absolute oral bioavailability or matched oral-versus-IV exposure data are available.",
    "No cirrhosis-specific pharmacokinetic data exist for the query molecule or a close structural analog; the only cirrhosis-matched record is meptazinol, a different scaffold.",
    "No direct measurements of query absorption, first-pass metabolism, solubility/dissolution, or transporter/efflux effects are available.",
    "L3 oral exposure records are for unrelated reference molecules and lack IV comparators, so they cannot establish absolute oral bioavailability for the query.",
    "The physicochemical prior is mixed (high MW/TPSA/charge versus moderate logD and no HBD) and cannot by itself establish the endpoint."
  ],
  "decision_summary": "Predicted high because all available threshold-relevant records, including the only cirrhosis-matched absolute F (meptazinol 27.9 ± 5.3%) and multiple direct human absolute F values, are at or above the 20% threshold; L3 oral exposure records are not applicable to the query and do not provide affirmative F < 20% evidence. Confidence remains moderate due to the lack of query-specific PK data and structural differences from the supporting contexts."
}

